    "## Implementation from Scratch\n",
    "\n",
    "Now, let's try implementing weight decay from scratch.\n",
    "Since minibatch stochastic gradient descent\n",
    "is our optimizer,\n",
    "we just need to add the squared $\\ell_2$ penalty\n",
    "to the original loss function.\n",
    "\n",
    "### (**Defining $\\ell_2$ Norm Penalty**)\n",
    "\n",
    "Perhaps the most convenient way to implement this penalty\n",
    "is to square all terms in place and sum them up.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 38,
   "id": "4dc880ed",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.772766Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.765343Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.776914Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.776069Z"
    },
    "origin_pos": 9,
    "tab": [
     "pytorch"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "def l2_penalty(w):\n",
    "    return (w ** 2).sum() / 2"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "0619f91b",
   "metadata": {
    "origin_pos": 10
   },
   "source": [
    "### Defining the Model\n",
    "\n",
    "In the final model,\n",
    "the linear regression and the squared loss have not changed since :numref:`sec_linear_scratch`,\n",
    "so we will just define a subclass of `d2l.LinearRegressionScratch`. The only change here is that our loss now includes the penalty term.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 39,
   "id": "4e57c6d5",
   "metadata": {
    "execution": {
     "iopub.execute_input": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.780837Z",
     "iopub.status.busy": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.780406Z",
     "iopub.status.idle": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.790261Z",
     "shell.execute_reply": "2023-02-10T05:17:57.789100Z"
    },
    "origin_pos": 11,
    "tab": [
     "pytorch"
    ]
   },
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class WeightDecayScratch(LinearRegressionScratch):\n",
    "    def __init__(self, num_inputs, lambd, lr, sigma=0.01):\n",
    "        super().__init__(num_inputs, lr, sigma)\n",
    "        self.save_hyperparameters()\n",
    "\n",
    "    def loss(self, y_hat, y):\n",
    "        return (super().loss(y_hat, y) +\n",
    "                self.lambd * l2_penalty(self.w))"
   ]
  },
